  "result": "I graded Leo's submission and wrote `grades/0001-s1.json`. Leo got 2 items correct, 1 partial and 1 wrong.\n\n- **q1 (follow-through): correct.** The follow-through is the kicking leg continuing toward the target after contact.\n- **q2 (penalty mark distance): correct.** Leo answered 12 yards, which is about 11 m, so the key counts it.\n- **q3 (five parts): partial.** Run-up, plant and follow-through are right and in order. \"Kick the ball\" skips the striking surface and the contact point as two separate steps.\n- **q4 (plant foot): wrong, M2.** Leo chose to plant well behind the ball for a longer swing. That habit likely explains the shots lifting over the bar. The plant foot belongs beside the ball, roughly level with it.\n\nI also added `learning-records/0002-plant-foot-misconception.md` and updated `NOTES.md`.\n\n**Next step:** at the next practice, take five kicks with the plant foot level with the ball. Compare where they finish with the usual behind-the-ball plant. I can write a short lesson on plant foot placement, striking surface and contact point if you'd like one.",
